narios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the failure semantics of the inline archive-time fold: on fold failure, archive must abort (not write ARCHIVED/marker) so no archived-but-unfolded ticket is created, relying on compact_txn's transaction boundary.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T7","T9"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.749,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"make the fold part of the archive operation itself: rebar archive performs the ticket's final fold inline ... right before writing the ARCHIVED event\"","Plan reuses \"the existing single-ticket fold path compact_txn already exposes\" but does not state fold-failure behavior for the archive path","New write-path failure point: fold precedes ARCHIVED event write"],"finding":"Change 1 adds an inline fold as a new step in the archive write operation, but the plan does not state what happens if that fold fails partway (e.g. SNAPSHOT partially written) before the ARCHIVED event — whether archive aborts atomically or leaves partial state.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa3bc8e09b44bd410","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 / Scope: src/rebar/_commands/leaf.py","norm_id":"ncf5d9e86597efbb3","priority":0.201,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The inline fold raises (corrupt event, I/O error) during archive — is the ARCHIVED event/marker still written, leaving an archived-but-unfolded ticket that the default sweep will now never revisit?"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to Approach step 1 confirming the inline fold runs inside/around compact_txn's transaction and that archive aborts (surfacing the error, no ARCHIVED event) if the fold fail