forcement placed in the CLI command is bypassed by the other two"],"finding":"The archive-time inline fold is placed in the CLI command module (`src/rebar/_commands/leaf.py`, `leaf.archive`) rather than in the shared archive write seam. If `rebar archive` is also reachable via an MCP tool handler or a library facade, those ingress paths write the ARCHIVED event without performing the inline fold, re-introducing the stranded-unfolded-events condition that the default active-only scan scoping (change 2) relies on being eliminated.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6c3fd41321b7f0c7","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 / Scope: 'src/rebar/_commands/leaf.py — archive performs the ticket's terminal fold inline before the ARCHIVED event.'","norm_id":"n66ab84202157ed19","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An MCP archive tool call writes ARCHIVED without the inline fold, leaving unfolded tail events on a ticket the default scan then skips — the events are stranded until a --include-archived sweep","A library facade archive() writes ARCHIVED without the inline fold, same stranding, silently defeating the 'archived ticket really IS folded on its way out' guarantee the default scoping depends on"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Move the fold-then-ARCHIVED sequencing into the shared `*_core` archive function that all three ingress paths call, leaving `leaf.py` to only invoke it; confirm the MCP archive handler and any `rebar.archive` facade route through the same core.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachab